# Zenrows

> Zenrows is web data infrastructure built for AI agents and applications. It gives them reliable access to the live web, including the protected web: sites defended by anti-bot systems, rendered in JavaScript, or built to block ordinary tools. Five primitives do the work: Fetch, Extract, Crawl (New), Batch and Browser Sessions. Each runs over the API, the CLI, MCP or an SDK.

The Zenrows HTTP API serves Fetch and Extract (`extract=auto`) at `https://api.zenrows.com/v1/`, Crawl (New) at `https://api.zenrows.com/v1/crawls`, and Batch at `https://async.api.zenrows.com/v1`. Fetch, Extract, Crawl and Batch are described in OpenAPI 3.1 at https://www.zenrows.com/openapi.json and listed in the RFC 9727 API catalog at https://www.zenrows.com/.well-known/api-catalog. Use the spec for exact parameter names and types. Browser Sessions connects your own Puppeteer or Playwright code over WebSocket.

No API key is needed to start: the local MCP server (`npx -y @zenrows/mcp`) and the CLI (`npx -y @zenrows/cli`) create a Free account (5,000 credits per month) on first use, which a person can claim later with the same key ([Agent signup and unclaimed accounts](https://docs.zenrows.com/authentication.md)). An agent can also pay per request with no account at all ([Agentic Payments](https://docs.zenrows.com/first-steps/agentic-payments.md)).

This file is a curated index of every page in the navigation, and each link points to that page's Markdown version. The full text of every page is in [llms-full.txt](https://docs.zenrows.com/llms-full.txt), and these docs can be searched over MCP at `https://docs.zenrows.com/mcp`.

## Get started

- [Welcome to Zenrows](https://docs.zenrows.com/first-steps/welcome.md): The primitives (Fetch, Extract, Crawl, Batch, Browser Sessions) and the surfaces they run on.
- [What is Zenrows?](https://docs.zenrows.com/first-steps/what-is-zenrows.md): What Zenrows is and why teams and AI agents use it for reliable web access.
- [How to Use Zenrows](https://docs.zenrows.com/first-steps/how-to-use-zenrows.md): Get an API key, then the setup guide for Fetch, Extract, Crawl, Batch or Browser Sessions on each surface.
- [Zenrows' Primitives](https://docs.zenrows.com/first-steps/our-products.md): Compare Fetch, Extract, Crawl, Batch and Browser Sessions and pick the right one.
- [Quick Setup and First Request](https://docs.zenrows.com/first-steps/getting-started-guide.md): Create an account, get your API key, send your first request.
- [Zenrows Pricing](https://docs.zenrows.com/first-steps/pricing.md): Plans, credits, cost multipliers, pay-per-success billing and the shared balance.
- [Agentic Payments](https://docs.zenrows.com/first-steps/agentic-payments.md): AI agents buy and call Fetch and Extract at agents.zenrows.com over x402, MPP or a card, with no Zenrows account.
- [Zenrows API Reference](https://docs.zenrows.com/api-reference.md): Every developer resource in one place: OpenAPI spec, authentication, SDKs and MCP.
- [Zenrows API Authentication](https://docs.zenrows.com/authentication.md): Where to find your API key, how to send it to each API and the MCP server, and how agent-created accounts are claimed.
- [API Error Codes](https://docs.zenrows.com/api-error-codes.md): Every API error code, what it means and the fix.
- [API Versioning and Deprecation](https://docs.zenrows.com/api-versioning.md): How versions are retired, with twelve months' notice.

## Fetch

Fetch (formerly, Universal Scraper API) gets any page as clean content: `GET https://api.zenrows.com/v1/` plus parameters.

- [Fetch API Reference](https://docs.zenrows.com/fetch/api-reference.md): Every Fetch parameter, authentication and pricing.
- [Setting Up Fetch](https://docs.zenrows.com/fetch/setup.md): API key, authentication and a first request.
- [Make Your First Request](https://docs.zenrows.com/fetch/first-request.md): First call in Python, Node.js, Go, Java, PHP, Ruby or cURL.
- [Common Use Cases & Recipes](https://docs.zenrows.com/fetch/common-use-cases.md): Ready-to-use recipes for anti-bot bypass, rendering and extraction.
- Anti-bot and proxies: [Adaptive Stealth Mode](https://docs.zenrows.com/fetch/features/adaptive-stealth-mode.md) (`mode=auto` picks the cheapest configuration that succeeds), [premium proxy](https://docs.zenrows.com/fetch/features/premium-proxy.md), [proxy country](https://docs.zenrows.com/fetch/features/proxy-country.md), [custom headers](https://docs.zenrows.com/fetch/features/headers.md).
- Rendering: [JavaScript rendering](https://docs.zenrows.com/fetch/features/js-rendering.md), [wait](https://docs.zenrows.com/fetch/features/wait.md), [wait for a selector](https://docs.zenrows.com/fetch/features/wait-for.md), [JavaScript instructions](https://docs.zenrows.com/fetch/features/js-instructions.md) (click, fill, scroll), [block resources](https://docs.zenrows.com/fetch/features/block-resources.md).
- Output: [JSON response](https://docs.zenrows.com/fetch/features/json-response.md) (with captured XHR), [Markdown](https://docs.zenrows.com/fetch/features/markdown.md), [plain text](https://docs.zenrows.com/fetch/features/plaintext.md), [PDF](https://docs.zenrows.com/fetch/features/pdf.md), [screenshot](https://docs.zenrows.com/fetch/features/screenshot.md), [output filters](https://docs.zenrows.com/fetch/features/output-filters.md), [CSS extractor](https://docs.zenrows.com/fetch/features/css-extractor.md), [download files](https://docs.zenrows.com/fetch/features/downloadfile.md), [Autoparse](https://docs.zenrows.com/fetch/features/autoparse.md) (deprecated in favor of Extract).
- [Concurrency](https://docs.zenrows.com/fetch/features/concurrency.md): Plan concurrency limits and parallel requests.
- [Other Features](https://docs.zenrows.com/fetch/features/other.md): Session ID, original status codes and POST requests.
- [Fetch FAQ](https://docs.zenrows.com/fetch/faq.md): Cookies, sessions, proxies and output formats.
- Troubleshooting: [basic guide](https://docs.zenrows.com/fetch/troubleshooting/troubleshooting-guide.md), [IP blocked or connection refused](https://docs.zenrows.com/fetch/troubleshooting/ip-address-blocked.md), [partial or empty responses](https://docs.zenrows.com/fetch/troubleshooting/empty-or-partialresponses.md), [proxy and geolocation](https://docs.zenrows.com/fetch/troubleshooting/troubleshooting-premium-proxies.md), [response too large (`413`)](https://docs.zenrows.com/fetch/troubleshooting/response-too-large.md), [advanced CSS selectors](https://docs.zenrows.com/fetch/troubleshooting/advanced-css-selectors.md), [CSS selector examples](https://docs.zenrows.com/fetch/troubleshooting/advanced-css-selector-examples.md).

## Extract

Extract turns a page into structured JSON: add `extract=auto` to a Fetch call.

- [Introduction to Extract](https://docs.zenrows.com/extract/introduction.md): A tailored extraction per website, kept working when layouts change.
- [Extract Setup](https://docs.zenrows.com/extract/setup.md): Make an Extract request and read the result.
- [Extract API Reference](https://docs.zenrows.com/extract/endpoints.md): Which domains are served, and how to request a new one.

## Crawl (New)

Crawl takes one start URL and returns the pages it finds: `https://api.zenrows.com/v1/crawls`.

- [Introduction to Crawl](https://docs.zenrows.com/crawl/introduction.md): How a crawl follows links from one start URL, and a first request.
- [Crawl Setup](https://docs.zenrows.com/crawl/setup.md): Start a crawl, read results with a cursor, download them, get each page's HTML, stop it.
- [Crawl Endpoints](https://docs.zenrows.com/crawl/endpoints.md): Parameters, response fields, statuses, limits, pricing and errors.

## Batch

Batch runs large lists of URLs as one managed job: `https://async.api.zenrows.com/v1`.

- [Introduction to Batch](https://docs.zenrows.com/batch/introduction.md): Submit a job, track it and collect the results.
- [Setting Up Batch](https://docs.zenrows.com/batch/setup.md): Authenticate, submit a first job and retrieve results.
- [Batch API Reference](https://docs.zenrows.com/batch/developer-guide-restapi.md): Every Batch request over HTTP, in seven languages.
- [Batch Troubleshooting](https://docs.zenrows.com/batch/troubleshooting.md): Submission errors, job states, downloads, webhooks and scheduling.
- [Batch FAQ](https://docs.zenrows.com/batch/faq.md): Access, pricing, limits, options and results.

## Browser Sessions

Browser Sessions (formerly, Scraping Browser) is a cloud browser for pages that need real interaction, driven by your own CDP code.

- [Introduction to Browser Sessions](https://docs.zenrows.com/browser-sessions/introduction.md): What it offers: residential proxies, geo-targeting and CDP.
- [Setting Up Browser Sessions](https://docs.zenrows.com/browser-sessions/setup.md): Connection URL and parameters for Puppeteer or Playwright.
- [Browser Sessions with Puppeteer](https://docs.zenrows.com/browser-sessions/get-started/puppeteer.md): Node.js and Pyppeteer.
- [Browser Sessions with Playwright](https://docs.zenrows.com/browser-sessions/get-started/playwright.md): Python and Node.js.
- [World Region](https://docs.zenrows.com/browser-sessions/features/world-region.md): Route a session through one world region.
- [Country Targeting](https://docs.zenrows.com/browser-sessions/features/country.md): Route a session through one country.
- [Session TTL](https://docs.zenrows.com/browser-sessions/features/session-ttl.md): Keep a session alive from 1 to 15 minutes.
- [Practical Use Cases](https://docs.zenrows.com/browser-sessions/help/practical-use-cases.md): Screenshots, forms, infinite scroll and network interception.
- [Browser Sessions FAQ](https://docs.zenrows.com/browser-sessions/faq.md): Sessions, CDP, proxies and limits.

## CLI

- [Zenrows CLI](https://docs.zenrows.com/cli/introduction.md): Install, authenticate and get a first result from the terminal.
- [CLI: fetch](https://docs.zenrows.com/cli/fetch/introduction.md): Get any page as clean content from the terminal.
- [CLI: extract](https://docs.zenrows.com/cli/extract/introduction.md): Structured JSON, chosen fields or Markdown from the terminal.
- [CLI: crawl](https://docs.zenrows.com/cli/crawl/introduction.md): Collect the URLs behind one start page, and each page's HTML on request.
- [CLI: batch](https://docs.zenrows.com/cli/batch/introduction.md): Run thousands of URLs as one job, with a cost check first.
- [CLI: browser](https://docs.zenrows.com/cli/browser/introduction.md): Drive a real browser when simpler methods can't.
- [Agent Toolkit](https://docs.zenrows.com/cli/agent-toolkit-overview.md): MCP, Skills, Templates, Workflows, Recipes and Evals for AI agents.
- Agent Toolkit pieces: [MCP config](https://docs.zenrows.com/cli/mcp.md), [Skills](https://docs.zenrows.com/cli/skills.md), [Templates](https://docs.zenrows.com/cli/templates.md), [Workflows](https://docs.zenrows.com/cli/workflows.md), [Recipes](https://docs.zenrows.com/cli/recipes.md) (double as smoke tests), [Evals](https://docs.zenrows.com/cli/evals.md).
- [CLI Troubleshooting](https://docs.zenrows.com/cli/troubleshooting.md): Read a run's trace and the next step for every error code.

